Summary:
During today’s session, the focus was on improving the frontend design of the Developer Portfolio Evaluator application. The existing user interface was refined to enhance visual clarity and user experience. Basic styling was added to elements such as input fields, buttons, and result sections to create a more structured and appealing layout. Efforts were made to improve alignment, spacing, and overall presentation without altering the core functionality. The interface was adjusted to ensure better readability and smoother interaction for users.

Outcomes:
By the end of the session, the application had a cleaner and more user-friendly interface. The improved design made it easier to navigate and understand the displayed results. Enhanced styling contributed to a more professional look and feel of the application. The changes did not affect the underlying functionality, ensuring stability while improving usability. Overall, the frontend became more presentable and aligned with basic UI/UX principles.
